Why Is Demand Increasing?
Vehicle electrification: Electric vehicles require microcontrollers for battery management, power conversion, and control systems.
Advanced driver assistance: Driver-assistance functions depend on electronic control and real-time processing.
Software-defined vehicles: Increasing vehicle functionality raises demand for capable and reliable embedded processors.
Connected-car features: Infotainment, body electronics, and vehicle networking create additional MCU applications.
Fab & Technology Pulse: Automotive Electronics Increase Computing Requirements

Automotive MCUs execute control instructions and process sensor inputs across vehicle subsystems. Product selection depends on processing performance, memory, power consumption, safety requirements, operating temperature, and communication interfaces.

Manufacturers are focusing on functional safety, cybersecurity, integration, and reliable operation under harsh automotive conditions. Long product lifecycles and automotive qualification requirements make supply-chain resilience and component availability important considerations.

